# BEAR CRAWL

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Bear Crawl is a quadrupedal locomotion exercise designed to develop whole-body coordination, dynamic trunk stability, shoulder robustness and movement efficiency.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-value locomotion exercises for developing integrated athletic movement.

---

# Philosophy

Elite movement is not built only while standing.

Quadrupedal movement develops coordination patterns that reinforce whole-body integration, stability and force transmission.

CAS selects the Bear Crawl whenever integrated movement quality is a priority.

